# Local memory-store data (personal agent-memory SQLite DBs and backups) —
# never commit and never package; leaked once into the sdist via the tracked
# data/ directory (untracked 2026-08-22).
# Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored "data/" also matches the
# lummenna/data/ source package, which silently hid new modules from git.
/data/

# Internal / local-only documentation and assets (not for public repo)
# NOTE: AGENTS.md is intentionally TRACKED — it is the enforced engineering
# constitution (No-Vaporware / No-False-Claims) that coding agents load every
# session and CI references. Keeping it out of the repo would defeat its purpose.
/docs/
dev-docs/
docs/internal/
.opencode/
ios/

# Per-developer OpenCode config. The working config must point at a real
# interpreter, so in practice it holds absolute machine-specific paths (a
# .venv/bin/python, a local browser binary). This repository is intended to
# become public, and until 2026-09-10 this file was untracked but NOT ignored,
# so any `git add -A` would have committed those paths verbatim.
#
# Ignoring it also protects it: `git clean -fd` removes untracked files but
# respects .gitignore, so only `git clean -fdx` can now delete your config.
#
# The portable, checked-in template contributors should copy is
# integrations/opencode/opencode.json.
/opencode.json
/opencode.jsonc
tmp/
lummenna/benchmarks/*/results/

# Local Lummenna runtime store + provisioned models (per-machine, never committed)
.lummenna/

# Wrangler's local state cache (local D1 shards, build metadata). Per-machine
# and regenerated on demand; committing it would leak local database contents.
# wrangler.toml itself IS tracked: it is the source of truth for Pages bindings.
.wrangler/

# Internal documentation. Brand bible, technical documentation, technical
# summary, whitepaper, key custody runbook, CLA and status notes are kept on
# disk but must not be tracked: this repository is intended to become public and
# these are internal or commercially sensitive.
#
# WARNING, and the reason this comment is worded carefully: a .gitignore entry
# has NO effect on a file that is already tracked. Until 2026-09-01 this block
# claimed the directory had been "untracked via `git rm -r --cached docs/`", but
# that had only ever been done on `main` (1 file). This branch still tracked 9,
# including LICENSE_SIGNING_KEY_CUSTODY.md and the CLA ownership attestation, so
# the entry below was silently doing nothing for them and the comment gave false
# assurance. They were untracked on 2026-09-01; verify with `git ls-files docs/`,
# which must print nothing, rather than trusting this comment.
#
# Untracking removes them from future commits only. The blobs remain reachable
# in history (30 paths across all refs) and still require a history rewrite
# before this repository is made public. See WEB-DEPLOYMENT.md.
docs/
branch_structure.json
config.bat
node_modules
